a dog has a name (text), an age (a number) and a good boy (yes or no).
let dogs be a list of (a new dog with name "Rex", age 3 and good boy yes), (a new dog with name "Bella", age 12 and good boy no) and (a new dog with name "Fido the Third", age 1 and good boy yes).
say dogs as a table.
say dogs sorted by age as a table.
say dogs sorted by age biggest first as a table.
let ages be a map of "Rex" to 3, "Bella" to 12 and "Café" to 1.
say ages as a table.
say (a list of 1, 22 and 333) as a table.
say (a list of "a", "bb" and "ccc") as a table.
say (an empty list of dogs) as a table.
say "[(an empty map from text to numbers) as a table]" is "".
let empty dogs be an empty list of dogs.
say empty dogs sorted by age.
